WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.230
Film Courage: What thoughts do you have for
people who are having trouble getting their

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.010
scripts out there and getting seen, getting
read.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.259
What advice do you have?

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:10.759
Writer/Director/Actor/Producer, Barney Cheng:
I’m having the same problem.

00:00:10.759 --> 00:00:17.060
I think the problem is finding the right person
to send it to.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:21.340
If your script is about a mystery you’re
not going to sending it to a romantic comedy

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.290
company.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:30.430
Each of our stories is so specific and so
authentic to our experiences, you just have

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.790
to find the right match.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:37.610
Once you find the right match then it’s
great.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:43.630
I think the homework (your work) in addition
to finishing the story and getting the story

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:51.180
in the best shape possible the next step is
to find the right company or the person to

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:58.840
send it to so the frustration probably comes
from that, sending it to the wrong people,

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:01.440
not doing the homework to send to the right
people.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:05.681
Film Courage: Are you in this position now
or you’re working on it right now?

00:01:05.681 --> 00:01:08.970
Barney: Right now I am focusing on finishing
my project.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:15.740
I feel like it’s not good to send anything
out that is not ready.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:21.531
That’s another thing that a lot of people
(a mistake that people make) that they send

00:01:21.531 --> 00:01:24.010
out stuff that is not ready.

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:30.740
You have one chance so you better make sure
that the project is in amazing shape before

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:37.070
sending it out to people who are going to
consider your project.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:45.011
I am focusing on my feature film right now
with the script.

00:01:45.011 --> 00:01:46.011
When it’s ready then I will send it out.

00:01:46.011 --> 00:01:47.070
Film Courage: Do you have an idea of when
it will be ready?

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:54.910
Barney: I give myself this rewriting process
by the end of September so I have about three

00:01:54.910 --> 00:02:02.150
months to finish rewriting the script and
then probably a couple of rewrites before

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:04.690
I send it out so this is my second rewrite.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:07.580
Film Courage: Will you give this to anyone
else to look over?

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:12.610
Barney: I will send it to…I have a group
of people that I trust.

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:22.230
I will send it to a handful of people that
I trust who will give me truthful, authentic

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:25.440
advice and feedback.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:32.450
Don’t give it to people, your family members
who always say good things about it.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:37.430
Don’t give it to actors who want to be in
the film, you know what I mean?

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:43.840
Just make sure that those people have no conflict
or any kind of vested interest in being in

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.740
the project (whatever).

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:50.959
Someone you trust, someone who knows what
they are talking about.

00:02:50.959 --> 00:02:57.210
I have about five or six people like that
who would give me their authentic, real, advice

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.110
and feedback that are constructive.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.230
Film Courage: Are they also writers?

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:04.190
Barney: Some writers, some actors, some producers.

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:05.200
Question for the viewers: Which is harder,
writing the screenplay or getting someone

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:05.440
to read it?

